/-!
# Finite presentation lifts along a square-zero reduction of a flat module

Let `(C, J)` be a site carrying two sheaves of commutative rings and a map `π : O ⟶ R` which is
locally surjective and whose kernel `I = ker π` is square zero. Let `ℱ'` be an `O`-module, let `𝒢`
be an `R`-module and let `q : ℱ' ⟶ 𝒢` be a `π`-semilinear map which is locally surjective and
whose kernel is locally `I·ℱ'`; so `𝒢` is the reduction `ℱ'/Iℱ'` of `ℱ'`. Assume that relations
`∑ dₖ eₖ = 0` among sections of `ℱ'` with coefficients `dₖ ∈ I` vanish trivially, in the sense
of the equational criterion for the vanishing of `∑ dₖ ⊗ eₖ` in `I ⊗ ℱ'`
(`Deformation.ToposThickening.ReductionPresentation.IdealRelationsVanish`). Then if `𝒢` is of
finite presentation over `R`, the module `ℱ'` is of finite presentation over `O`.

This is the hard direction (2) ⇒ (1) of Stacks 08VU, with "we may and do assume `C = C'`" of the
source's proof carried out: everything here lives on one site. The hypothesis on relations is
what the source extracts from the injectivity of `I ⊗_O ℱ ⟶ ℱ'` (Stacks 08MQ); it also holds when
`ℱ'` is flat over a third sheaf of rings `ρ : A ⟶ O` whose image generates `I` locally (the form
strictness of a morphism of thickenings, Stacks 08M9, takes on sections), by the local equational
criterion for flatness (Stacks 08FC).

## Main results

* `Deformation.ToposThickening.ReductionPresentation.isFinitePresentation_of_reduction`: the
  statement above.
* `Deformation.ToposThickening.ReductionPresentation.idealRelationsVanish_of_isFlat`: relations
  with coefficients in `I` vanish trivially in a module flat over `A` when `I` is generated by the
  image of `A`.
* `Deformation.ToposThickening.ReductionPresentation.locally_isSectionPresentation_of_reduction`:
  the local lifting of a presentation, on one object.

## How the proof goes

The source's proof: locally present `𝒢` by `O^m ⟶ O^n ⟶ 𝒢 ⟶ 0`, lift the generators to `ℱ'` and the
relations to `O`, correct the lifted relations by elements of `I^{⊕n}` so that they become
relations among the lifted generators, and check exactness of the lifted presentation. The check is
done here on sections, in the shape
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_isFinite_presentation_over_of_relations` consumes: (A) the corrected
relations are relations, (B) the lifted generators generate locally, and (C) every relation among
the lifted generators is locally a combination of the corrected relations.

(B) is Nakayama for a square-zero ideal: a section killed by `q` is locally of the form
`∑ cᵢ yᵢ` with `cᵢ ∈ I`, each `yᵢ` is a combination of the generators up to a further element of
the kernel, and that further element is killed by `cᵢ` because `I² = 0`.

(C) is where the hypothesis on relations enters, in place of the source's appeal to the
injectivity of `I ⊗_O ℱ ⟶ ℱ'`. Given a relation `a` among the lifted generators `s`, its reduction
is a relation among the generators of `𝒢`, so after subtracting a combination of the corrected
relations it becomes a relation `d` with coefficients in `I`. The relation `∑ dₖ sₖ = 0` vanishes
trivially: `sₖ = ∑_g βₖ_g τ_g` with `∑_g κ_gₚ τ_g = 0` and `∑ₖ βₖ_g dₖ = ∑ₚ κ_gₚ uₚ`, `uₚ ∈ I`.
Writing the `τ_g` in terms of `s`, the vectors `κₚ` read in `s` are relations among `s`, hence
combinations of the corrected relations up to vectors in `I^{⊕n}`, which are killed by `uₚ ∈ I`;
substituting back exhibits `d`, hence `a`, as a combination of the corrected relations. When `ℱ'`
is flat over `A`, the trivial vanishing comes from strictness, `dₖ = ∑ₚ βₖₚ ρ(αₚ)` with
`ρ(αₚ) ∈ I`, and the equational criterion applied to `∑ₚ αₚ • (∑ₖ βₖₚ sₖ) = 0`.

## Implementation notes

All statements are about sections and covering sieves; no free sheaf, kernel or tensor product
of sheaves is formed until the decoding step at the very end. "Holds on a covering sieve" is the
predicate `Deformation.ToposThickening.ReductionPresentation.Locally`, with a `bind` rule for
refining a covering on each of its members and a rule for intersecting finitely many coverings.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08VU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08VU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08M9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08M9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
-/

